# Commentary III: Geography as Text and Context: An Australian Perspective.

**Authors:** Powell, Joe

## Abstract
Contends that the division between the science and humanities inhibit the use of qualitative research in Australian college-level geography instruction. Argues that qualitative methods might be more acceptable in cultural and historical geography. Suggests that philosophy courses or foundations courses in the humanities and social sciences might provide a forum for discussing qualitative research methods. (CFR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ467805

